        "id": 1125984
      },
      "writtenOn": "2017-04-22T01:29:07Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "My understanding is that a PDU is the payload and header (struct upgrade_command). If that\u0027s correct, we should probably state that clearly.\n\n\"Image transfer is done in up to 1K sized protocol data units (PDUs)\". \"The host supplying the image encapsulates blocks with the upgrade_command header forming an update PDU.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 19,
        "startChar": 1,
        "endLine": 21,
        "endChar": 53
      },
      "revId": "c73af7dd243c7b32c75fbeb29b22ba15c412eb5a",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
