    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "b7a29f40_a1de5dad",
        "filename": "chip/g/upgrade_fw.h",
        "patchSetId": 7
      },
      "lineNbr": 21,
      "author": {
        "id": 1129199
      },
      "writtenOn": "2017-04-24T04:59:45Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Not quite, I think the current text is correct. _Blocks_ (aka payload/raw data) are indeed 1K long. In front of each block, there is a header (upgrade_command) to indicate the payload address. The whole thing is a PDU (so that\u0027s 1K+8 bytes long). Then the PDU can be further encapsulated/split in frames.",
      "parentUuid": "c855c05f_50318d6a",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 19,
        "startChar": 1,
        "endLine": 21,
        "endChar": 53
      },
      "revId": "c73af7dd243c7b32c75fbeb29b22ba15c412eb5a",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
